              "text": "{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"stdout\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\\section{Experimental Setup}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{Models and Datasets}\\\\n\\\\nWe use \\\\\\\\textbf{Pythia-410M-deduped} (405M parameters, $D{=}1024$) as the primary model and \\\\\\\\textbf{Pythia-1B-deduped} (1042M parameters, $D{=}2048$) for scale-transfer validation.\\\\nBoth are decoder-only transformers pretrained on the deduplicated Pile.\\\\n\\\\nFrom the Pile (uncopyrighted split, \\\\\\\\texttt{monology/pile-uncopyrighted}), we sample three disjoint subsets:\\\\n\\\\\\\\begin{itemize}[nosep]\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Training pool}: 50{,}000 sequences of 512 tokens for fine-tuning.\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Evaluation set}: 5{,}000 held-out sequences for perplexity measurement.\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Spectral probe set}: 1{,}000 held-out sequences for effective rank computation.\\\\n\\\\\\\\end{itemize}\\\\nAll sequences are tokenized with the GPTNeoX tokenizer (vocabulary size 50{,}304) and truncated or padded to 512 tokens.\\\\nWe retain only sequences with at least 256 non-padding tokens ($\\\\\\\\geq$50\\\\\\\\% fill ratio) to ensure sufficient context for representation extraction.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{Recursive Training Protocol}\\\\n\\\\nGeneration~0 is the pretrained checkpoint with no additional fine-tuning.\\\\nFor each subsequent generation $t = 1, \\\\\\\\ldots, T$ with $T{=}10$:\\\\n\\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}[nosep]\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Synthetic generation.} Sample 50{,}000 sequences from $M_{t-1}$ via ancestral sampling (temperature $= 1.0$, top-$k = 50$, no nucleus filtering, max length 512 tokens, batch size 32).\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Data mixing.} Combine synthetic samples with real data at condition-specific ratio $r_t$ (see \\\\\\\\S\\\\\\\\ref{sec:conditions}).  The number of real samples mixed in is $\\\\\\\\lfloor n_{\\\\\\\\text{syn}} \\\\\\\\cdot r_t / (1 - r_t) \\\\\\\\rfloor$, drawn uniformly without replacement from the training pool.\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Fine-tuning.} Train $M_{t-1}$ for 1 epoch on the mixed corpus $\\\\\\\\rightarrow M_t$.\\\\n  \\\\\\\\item \\\n…[truncated 6942 chars]"
